w: Thy Sa- vior yields His breath. The Prince of Life * from hea- ven
w: Blood streams from e- very pore. Through grief whose depth * none know- eth,
w: And caused Thee all Thy woe? While we must make * con- fes- sion
w: As count- less as the sands. I caused the woes * un- num- bered
w: Bound hand and foot in hell. The fet- ters and * the scour- ging,
w: It crushed me to the ground. The cross for me _ en- du- ring,
w: That I might ran- somed be. My bond- sman, ev- _ er will- ing,
w: From such a mon- ster dire. My death a- way _ Thou ta- kest,
w: I am no long- er mine. To Thee I glad- _ ly ten- der
w: But one thing do I say: Thy death and sor- _ rows ev- er,
w: Wher- ev- er I may be; Thine in- no- cence _ re- veal- ing,
w: How loud His thun- ders roll, How fear- ful- ly _ He smi- teth,
w: My heart with qu- iet- ness, And how I still _ should love them
w: I'll curb my veng- eful heart. The un- just wrong _ I'll suf- fer,
